   "definition_quote": "We consider a bandit problem with a set ${\\cal A}\\subset \\mathbb{R}^d$ of arms. In round $t\\ge 1$, if the decision maker selects arm $a$, she observes as a feedback a random reward $r_t = \\mu^\\top a +\\eta_t$. ... $\\eta_t\\sim {\\cal N}(0,\\sigma)$. ... we assume that ... the best arm $a_\\mu^\\star$ is unique. We also assume that the set of arms ${\\cal A}$ spans $\\mathbb{R}^d$. ... Consider a finite set ${\\cal A}$ of $K$ arms."
